---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Posturely"
  description="Read how Posturely uses camera access for real-time on-device posture detection and why camera footage is not uploaded to Posturely servers."
  canonical="/privacy/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy policy"
    title="Clear information about camera use and posture detection."
    description="This policy explains the privacy facts currently confirmed for Posturely. Items marked TODO require developer confirmation before publication."
  />
  <article class="policy">
    <div class="container policy-grid">
      <aside>
        <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy policy' }]} />
        <p>Last updated: August 31, 2026</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="policy-content">
        <section>
          <h2>1. About Posturely</h2>
          <p>Posturely is an iOS and iPadOS app that helps users become aware of visible upper-body posture changes during studying, reading, homework, and desk work.</p>
          <p>Posturely is not a medical product. It does not diagnose, treat, prevent, or measure medical conditions, and it does not provide medical advice.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>2. Camera access</h2>
          <p>Posturely requests camera access so it can perform real-time posture detection during an active monitoring session.</p>
          <p>Camera frames used for posture detection are processed on the device. Camera footage used for posture detection is not uploaded to Posturely servers.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>3. On-device posture processing</h2>
          <p>Posturely analyzes visible upper-body posture locally on your iPhone or iPad. The app may use this analysis to identify changes such as head-down posture, forward leaning, body tilt, or other noticeable posture changes and to provide reminders.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>4. Permissions</h2>
          <p>You can manage camera permission in iOS or iPadOS Settings. If camera access is disabled, features that require real-time posture detection cannot operate.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>5. Information that still requires confirmation</h2>
          <div class="todo surface-card">
            <strong>TODO before publication</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>Confirm whether the app collects diagnostics, crash reports, usage analytics, or device identifiers.</li>
              <li>Confirm what reminder history or settings are stored, where they are stored, and the applicable retention behavior.</li>
              <li>Confirm subscription and purchase data handling, including the role of Apple and any third-party purchase SDK.</li>
              <li>Confirm age requirements, children’s privacy treatment, governing law, and the legal developer identity.</li>
              <li>Confirm the public privacy contact email and effective date.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p>No statement about these topics should be inferred from this draft until the developer confirms the relevant implementation and legal requirements.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>6. Contact</h2>
          <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2rem 0 7rem;
  }

  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 250px minmax(0, 760px);
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  aside > p {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--subtle);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .policy-content section {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0 0 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.75rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 520;
  }

  .policy-content p,
  .policy-content li {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .policy-content a {
    color: var(--accent-text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .todo {
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    border-color: rgba(138, 90, 0, 0.25);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .todo strong {
    color: #8a5a00;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .todo ul {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
